  "id": "COMPOUND:29842 - PROTEIN:5866",
  "verbalization": "Taiwanin C appears to have a complex relationship with NCI-H446 through a series of target interactions involving 5-Oxobrucine. The evidence suggests that Taiwanin C directly targets Caspase-5 or Microtubule-associated protein 1B, both of which are subsequently targeted by 5-Oxobrucine. This chain of targets leads to NCI-H446, indicating a potential pathway through which Taiwanin C may influence the cell behavior of NCI-H446. The presence of multiple overlapping targets, including Caspase-5 and Microtubule-associated protein 1B, suggests that 5-Oxobrucine may act as a bridge in this relationship, possibly by modulating cellular processes that are critical for NCI-H446's function. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of 5-Oxobrucine in mediating the effect of Taiwanin C on NCI-H446, though the exact mechanism of action remains to be elucidated.",
